# Chandra, Pyromaster's +1 deals 1 damage to the target player and 1 to up to one target creature that player controls, and that
# creature can't block this turn. Turn 1: the second target may be left out (Bot2 takes 1, 19), and Bot1's own Ornithopter is
# refused as the second target while Bot2 is the first (the creature must be the player's). Turn 3: Bot2's Ornithopter is
# targeted too (Bot2 18, the Ornithopter has 1 damage) and, attacked by Bot1's Ornithopter, it can't block; on turn 5 the
# restriction is over and the same block is allowed (the refusal beside its positive control).

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Chandra, Pyromaster
Ornithopter
Island x3
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Chandra, Pyromaster.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Chandra, Pyromaster.Activate(Ability: +1)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Chandra, Pyromaster.Activate(Ability: +1)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 18
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 1
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Blockers]
! Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Ornithopter)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Chandra, Pyromaster.Activate(Ability: +1)
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Blockers]
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Ornithopter)

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Battlefield.Chandra, Pyromaster.Counters.Loyalty = 7
